1
00:00:03,503 --> 00:00:06,506
But the fact is that the price
that Ukraine

2
00:00:07,140 --> 00:00:10,143
has paid up to now, and will pay

3
00:00:10,143 --> 00:00:13,413
in the future is much,

4
00:00:13,980 --> 00:00:18,051
much greater than the price
that the Russians have paid

5
00:00:18,051 --> 00:00:22,956
and the West is leading
Ukraine down the primrose

6
00:00:22,956 --> 00:00:27,093
path, and the Israelis
are executing a genocide in Gaza.

7
00:00:27,160 --> 00:00:30,830
It's not China's fault
that it wants to be powerful.

8
00:00:30,864 --> 00:00:33,833
So if you get into trouble and you

9
00:00:33,833 --> 00:00:38,905
dial 911, there's nobody at the other...
Hi, this is John Mearsheimer,

10
00:00:39,305 --> 00:00:43,076
and in today's episode,
what I would like to talk about

11
00:00:43,109 --> 00:00:47,781
is an article that appeared in Britain

12
00:00:48,248 --> 00:00:51,951
that was written by Yulia Mendel.

13
00:00:52,018 --> 00:00:55,388
And it's entitled "Zelensky's Strategy

14
00:00:55,522 --> 00:00:58,425
Is National Suicide."

15
00:00:58,425 --> 00:01:02,796
And this article was published
in The Spectator,

16
00:01:02,796 --> 00:01:07,033
which is a British magazine,
on the 15th of September.

17
00:01:07,067 --> 00:01:09,169
That was a week ago today.

18
00:01:09,169 --> 00:01:14,074
And then the day
after she actually gave a speech.

19
00:01:14,074 --> 00:01:18,078
It was done
virtually to the European Parliament

20
00:01:18,078 --> 00:01:23,083
on the same basic themes
that are contained in that article.

21
00:01:23,683 --> 00:01:28,254
Now, who exactly is Yulia Mendel?

22
00:01:28,655 --> 00:01:29,456
She was,

23
00:01:30,824 --> 00:01:32,692
President Zelensky's

24
00:01:32,692 --> 00:01:38,198
first press secretary
between 2019 and 2021.

25
00:01:38,465 --> 00:01:41,267
And as I'm sure everyone knows, the war
in Ukraine

26
00:01:41,267 --> 00:01:44,270
broke out in February of 2022.

27
00:01:44,370 --> 00:01:47,874
So she was not the press secretary
when the war broke out.

28
00:01:47,974 --> 00:01:52,378
She was the press secretary
for the two years before the war.

29
00:01:52,378 --> 00:01:56,516
Nevertheless,
she remained very close to Zelensky

30
00:01:56,749 --> 00:02:01,354
and she was a firm supporter of the war
through 2024.

31
00:02:01,988 --> 00:02:06,893
But then in 2025,
she began to be a real doubter.

32
00:02:06,960 --> 00:02:10,096
She began to think that this war
made no sense,

33
00:02:10,630 --> 00:02:14,234
and she started to criticize the conflict.

34
00:02:14,300 --> 00:02:18,972
And this, of course,
resulted in the article that she wrote

35
00:02:18,972 --> 00:02:23,443
last week in The Spectator and the talk
that she gave to the European Parliament.

36
00:02:23,576 --> 00:02:28,414
Now I want to lay out
exactly what her specific argument is.

37
00:02:28,948 --> 00:02:34,554
She is not arguing
that Ukraine is going to lose the war,

38
00:02:35,722 --> 00:02:37,824
although she believes that's true.

39
00:02:37,824 --> 00:02:42,061
She says the Ukraine has no, quote
unquote, theory of victory.

40
00:02:42,095 --> 00:02:45,865
And it's clear from the piece
that she expects Russia to win the war.

41
00:02:46,099 --> 00:02:48,401
Her argument goes well beyond that.

42
00:02:48,401 --> 00:02:53,473
She's arguing that Ukraine
is actually committing national suicide,

43
00:02:53,940 --> 00:02:58,811
and she's arguing
that Ukraine is going to end up

44
00:02:58,912 --> 00:03:03,550
in a situation where it is
no longer a functioning state.

45
00:03:03,883 --> 00:03:09,789
It is completely dysfunctional
as a result of this war.

46
00:03:09,923 --> 00:03:13,059
I don't think she's arguing, quite wisely,

47
00:03:13,226 --> 00:03:16,262
I might add, that Ukraine
is going to disappear from the map.

48
00:03:16,262 --> 00:03:21,834
I think she recognizes that there will be
a dysfunctional rump state at the end,

49
00:03:22,068 --> 00:03:26,472
but that rump state
will be dysfunctional in the extreme.

50
00:03:26,472 --> 00:03:30,343
And I think that's what she means
by national suicide.

51
00:03:30,877 --> 00:03:35,815
I think that this is
a remarkably controversial argument,

52
00:03:35,949 --> 00:03:39,018
not simply because she's arguing

53
00:03:39,018 --> 00:03:42,055
that Zelensky is responsible

54
00:03:42,255 --> 00:03:48,461
for pushing Ukraine down this road,
but also because of her former position

55
00:03:48,461 --> 00:03:52,265
as his press secretary
and as a staunch supporter of the war.

56
00:03:52,298 --> 00:03:54,867
Up until 2025.

57
00:03:54,867 --> 00:03:57,303
So she's not just any person
off the street.

58
00:03:57,303 --> 00:04:01,774
She's an she's a person
of quite significant prominence,

59
00:04:01,774 --> 00:04:05,578
and she's making
a remarkably controversial argument.

60
00:04:06,012 --> 00:04:06,946
I think the argument

61
00:04:06,946 --> 00:04:11,618
is not only controversial,
but I think it's compelling as well.

62
00:04:11,618 --> 00:04:15,521
I think when you go through
all the different points

63
00:04:15,521 --> 00:04:19,993
that she makes in the piece,
it's quite clear that she's correct

64
00:04:19,993 --> 00:04:23,563
that Ukraine is committing
national suicide.

65
00:04:23,630 --> 00:04:26,666
And what I'd like to do
is go through her argument,

66
00:04:26,699 --> 00:04:31,271
unpack the claims
or the various points that she's making.

67
00:04:32,538 --> 00:04:32,872
And I

68
00:04:32,872 --> 00:04:36,109
think the best way to do
that is to start with a simple framework.

69
00:04:36,743 --> 00:04:39,345
And that framework says that in essence,

70
00:04:39,345 --> 00:04:42,348
there are five parts

71
00:04:42,348 --> 00:04:46,552
to her argument, five dimensions.

72
00:04:46,886 --> 00:04:49,756
One is that

73
00:04:49,756 --> 00:04:53,259
Ukraine is undergoing
a demographic disaster.

74
00:04:53,793 --> 00:04:58,631
Two, that Ukraine is undergoing
an economic disaster.

75
00:04:59,265 --> 00:05:04,737
Three, that Ukraine is undergoing
a territorial disaster.

76
00:05:05,171 --> 00:05:09,309
Four, that it's
undergoing a political disaster.

77
00:05:09,742 --> 00:05:14,180
And finally, number five,
it's undergoing a security disaster.

78
00:05:14,180 --> 00:05:16,883
So to be clear again,
there are five dimensions here

79
00:05:16,883 --> 00:05:18,151
that we want to talk about.

80
00:05:18,151 --> 00:05:20,253
One is the demographic disaster.

81
00:05:20,253 --> 00:05:23,189
Two is the economic disaster.

82
00:05:23,189 --> 00:05:27,226
Three is the territorial disaster
four is the political disaster.

83
00:05:27,393 --> 00:05:30,396
And five is the security disaster.

84
00:05:30,763 --> 00:05:33,299
Let me start
with the demographic disaster,

85
00:05:33,299 --> 00:05:39,272
which in many ways is, I think,
the most powerful part of her argument.

86
00:05:40,073 --> 00:05:44,410
She basically says that
if you look at what's happened to Ukraine

87
00:05:44,410 --> 00:05:50,149
since it got its independence in 1991,
which of course was not that long ago,

88
00:05:50,783 --> 00:05:54,721
its population has halved. Ukraine today

89
00:05:54,754 --> 00:06:00,426
has half the population that it had
when it got its independence in 1991.

90
00:06:00,960 --> 00:06:05,932
She also makes the argument
that half of the existing population

91
00:06:05,932 --> 00:06:09,869
inside of Ukraine is of retirement age.

92
00:06:10,670 --> 00:06:15,508
50% of the population
is of retirement age.

93
00:06:16,709 --> 00:06:18,010
Furthermore,

94
00:06:18,010 --> 00:06:21,514
she makes the point
which I find stunning that

95
00:06:21,547 --> 00:06:27,720
for every one birth in Ukraine these days,
there are four deaths.

96
00:06:27,954 --> 00:06:30,623
Just think about that: four people die

97
00:06:30,623 --> 00:06:34,093
for every one person
who is born in Ukraine.

98
00:06:34,627 --> 00:06:38,664
And then she looks
at the number of young men

99
00:06:38,998 --> 00:06:41,868
who are of conscription age

100
00:06:41,868 --> 00:06:45,505
in Russia and in Ukraine.

101
00:06:45,938 --> 00:06:49,442
And she makes the argument
that there are 4 million men

102
00:06:49,575 --> 00:06:52,478
in Ukraine of conscription age.

103
00:06:52,478 --> 00:06:56,416
And she argues that Russia has ten times

104
00:06:56,549 --> 00:06:59,552
as many people of conscription age.

105
00:06:59,786 --> 00:07:03,022
And of course, one of her
central arguments in this piece,

106
00:07:03,156 --> 00:07:07,360
which is not controversial at all,
is that this is a war of attrition.

107
00:07:07,360 --> 00:07:09,061
In a war of attrition,

108
00:07:09,061 --> 00:07:13,032
the size of your population matters
greatly, and the number of men

109
00:07:13,099 --> 00:07:16,836
you have of conscription age
obviously matters greatly.

110
00:07:16,869 --> 00:07:22,508
And she's arguing
that Russia has ten times as many people

111
00:07:22,542 --> 00:07:26,212
who are of conscription age
as Ukraine does.

112
00:07:26,913 --> 00:07:31,217
Now, I've checked up on her numbers
as best I can.

113
00:07:31,317 --> 00:07:35,054
And I think she's essentially correct
with regard to all those numbers

114
00:07:35,621 --> 00:07:38,157
on population size.

115
00:07:38,157 --> 00:07:42,862
Almost everybody agrees
that Ukraine was about comprised

116
00:07:42,862 --> 00:07:46,599
of about 52 million people
when it got its independence.

117
00:07:46,866 --> 00:07:50,102
Her argument
is that Ukraine now has between

118
00:07:50,102 --> 00:07:53,139
20 and 25 million people.

119
00:07:53,439 --> 00:07:59,345
So you see, if
if you use her upper end number

120
00:07:59,345 --> 00:08:04,317
25 million, 25 million is easily
half of 52 million.

121
00:08:04,517 --> 00:08:08,988
And if you use the number
20 million, it's more than half.

122
00:08:09,322 --> 00:08:14,360
In other words, Ukraine's
population has been cut by more than half.

123
00:08:14,560 --> 00:08:18,331
I think the 25 million number
is a better number to use.

124
00:08:18,764 --> 00:08:23,035
I think if you look at what
demographic demographers

125
00:08:23,035 --> 00:08:27,874
in Ukraine are saying,
they usually put the number in the high 20s

126
00:08:29,141 --> 00:08:30,543
range.

127
00:08:30,543 --> 00:08:33,613
They usually put the number around 28, 29.

128
00:08:33,846 --> 00:08:39,218
And if you look at official government
statistics, the principal minister

129
00:08:39,252 --> 00:08:42,255
of for social policy puts the number

130
00:08:42,622 --> 00:08:45,391
at between 22 and 25.

131
00:08:45,391 --> 00:08:48,394
So again her number is 20 to 25.

132
00:08:48,494 --> 00:08:53,799
And the Minister for Social Policy
puts the number at 22 to 25.

133
00:08:53,833 --> 00:08:56,502
I think 25 is a good number to use.

134
00:08:56,502 --> 00:09:00,373
And if you use the number 25,
which is to say

135
00:09:00,373 --> 00:09:03,776
there are 25 million people
in Ukraine today, then it's quite clear

136
00:09:03,776 --> 00:09:07,613
that that is half the population

137
00:09:07,613 --> 00:09:13,452
that existed in Ukraine in 1991
when it got its independence.

138
00:09:13,986 --> 00:09:19,158
With regard to the claim
that half of the population is

139
00:09:19,659 --> 00:09:22,495
of retirement age,
in other words, half of that

140
00:09:22,495 --> 00:09:25,498
25 million is of retirement age.

141
00:09:25,531 --> 00:09:29,335
I think the number
is probably closer to 45%, but

142
00:09:30,102 --> 00:09:33,773
there's not that much difference
between 45% and 50%.

143
00:09:33,873 --> 00:09:37,944
And on the point that she makes,
which I think again, is quite stunning,

144
00:09:38,010 --> 00:09:39,111
that there are four

145
00:09:40,112 --> 00:09:41,714
Ukrainians dying every

146
00:09:41,714 --> 00:09:44,984
day for every one Ukrainian who is born.

147
00:09:44,984 --> 00:09:46,652
I think that number is correct.

148
00:09:46,652 --> 00:09:50,122
I don't see any evidence that she's wrong
there.

149
00:09:50,222 --> 00:09:54,026
And the same thing is true with her
claim that there are

150
00:09:55,828 --> 00:09:58,931
4 million Ukrainians of draft age,

151
00:09:58,931 --> 00:10:02,868
and there are ten times
as many Russians of draft age.

152
00:10:03,002 --> 00:10:08,307
I would add the caveat, however, that
the Russians don't draft people

153
00:10:08,307 --> 00:10:12,678
and send them into combat
in the way that the Ukrainians do.

154
00:10:12,712 --> 00:10:17,717
But nevertheless,
I think her point about the ten times

155
00:10:17,717 --> 00:10:20,786
greater number of potential

156
00:10:20,786 --> 00:10:23,789
Russian conscripts is correct.

157
00:10:23,789 --> 00:10:28,861
Let me just add some facts
to what she had to say.

158
00:10:29,261 --> 00:10:32,098
Recently, the Polish

159
00:10:32,098 --> 00:10:35,101
Prime Minister, Donald Tusk, said

160
00:10:35,101 --> 00:10:38,104
that the Ukrainians are losing

161
00:10:38,437 --> 00:10:43,776
27,000 soldiers every month.

162
00:10:43,843 --> 00:10:47,480
Either to death or to wounds.

163
00:10:47,613 --> 00:10:52,718
In other words, the number of Ukrainian
casualties on a monthly basis.

164
00:10:52,785 --> 00:10:56,722
He was told by the Ukrainians,
this is what Prime Minister

165
00:10:56,822 --> 00:11:00,393
Tusk of
Poland says he was told by the Ukrainians,

166
00:11:00,559 --> 00:11:03,663
is that Ukraine is losing 27 million

167
00:11:03,796 --> 00:11:06,799
people per month.

168
00:11:07,199 --> 00:11:09,802
And again, that's casualties, not deaths.

169
00:11:09,802 --> 00:11:14,573
It's deaths plus wounded
and I would assume, badly wounded.

170
00:11:14,907 --> 00:11:19,779
Well,
this war has been going on for 54 months.

171
00:11:20,312 --> 00:11:23,582
And if you assume that
there were 27 million,

172
00:11:24,483 --> 00:11:27,186
excuse me, 27,000 casualties

173
00:11:27,186 --> 00:11:30,589
every month, then that would mean

174
00:11:30,589 --> 00:11:34,026
that over the course of these 54 months,
over the course of this war,

175
00:11:34,360 --> 00:11:39,598
the Ukrainians have suffered
1,458,000 casualties.

176
00:11:40,099 --> 00:11:44,937
Now, I think that number is inflated,
because I don't think that Ukraine

177
00:11:45,438 --> 00:11:48,441
has been losing 27,000,

178
00:11:48,607 --> 00:11:52,078
troops every month.

179
00:11:52,111 --> 00:11:56,115
In other words, there haven't been 27,000
casualties every month for this war.

180
00:11:56,148 --> 00:11:59,118
I think the number per month is lower.

181
00:11:59,118 --> 00:12:02,588
I can't tell you exactly
what the number is, but let's just assume

182
00:12:02,922 --> 00:12:06,492
that the Ukrainians have suffered
20,000 casualties

183
00:12:06,559 --> 00:12:10,396
per month,
not 27,000 casualties per month.

184
00:12:11,030 --> 00:12:13,799
Even if the Ukrainians are only suffering

185
00:12:13,799 --> 00:12:16,802
20,000 casualties per month.

186
00:12:16,869 --> 00:12:21,941
That would still be a total of more
than 1 million casualties.

187
00:12:21,974 --> 00:12:26,112
This is a remarkably high number,
and you want to remember that in the month

188
00:12:26,112 --> 00:12:29,515
of July of this year, President Zelensky

189
00:12:29,548 --> 00:12:32,785
said that only 50,000

190
00:12:33,352 --> 00:12:35,955
Ukrainians had died in this war

191
00:12:35,955 --> 00:12:38,958
and 400,000 had been wounded.

192
00:12:38,958 --> 00:12:42,094
So, according to President Zelensky,

193
00:12:42,094 --> 00:12:45,131
the number of casualties in this war

194
00:12:45,231 --> 00:12:48,801
on the Ukrainian side are 450,000

195
00:12:49,135 --> 00:12:52,338
450,000 is a lot less

196
00:12:52,671 --> 00:12:57,476
than the 1.458 million

197
00:12:57,510 --> 00:13:00,513
figure, and even a lot less,

198
00:13:00,980 --> 00:13:04,183
more than half
less than the 1 million figure.

199
00:13:04,183 --> 00:13:08,020
If you assume that there have been
only 20,000 casualties per month.

200
00:13:08,254 --> 00:13:12,191
So you can see the effects of this war
have been stunning.

201
00:13:12,625 --> 00:13:15,027
From a demographic point of view

202
00:13:15,995 --> 00:13:17,229
on Ukraine.

203
00:13:17,229 --> 00:13:21,133
There's one more point that needs to be
made regarding demography.

204
00:13:21,133 --> 00:13:24,436
Almost everybody
who has looked at this problem

205
00:13:24,904 --> 00:13:28,841
believes that Ukraine is going to have a

206
00:13:29,708 --> 00:13:32,077
an extremely difficult time

207
00:13:32,077 --> 00:13:35,748
recovering from this demographic disaster.

208
00:13:35,781 --> 00:13:38,784
In fact,
some argue that it's almost impossible.

209
00:13:38,784 --> 00:13:39,552
First of all,

210
00:13:39,552 --> 00:13:44,323
you have a much smaller population
now than you had before the war started.

211
00:13:44,890 --> 00:13:50,396
Number two, you have an old population,
and number three,

212
00:13:50,429 --> 00:13:55,100
you have a remarkably low
fertility rate inside of Ukraine.

213
00:13:55,301 --> 00:14:00,439
The average
Ukrainian woman basically has 1.0 babies.

214
00:14:00,973 --> 00:14:04,143
And to have replacement rate,

215
00:14:04,310 --> 00:14:07,947
it's essential
that each woman have 2.1 babies.

216
00:14:08,013 --> 00:14:11,116
That's just to maintain
a steady population number.

217
00:14:11,417 --> 00:14:15,521
But again,
Ukrainians are not even close to 2.1.

218
00:14:15,554 --> 00:14:17,723
The number is 1.0.

219
00:14:17,723 --> 00:14:22,361
So most people think
that this demographic disaster

220
00:14:22,728 --> 00:14:26,999
is not going to improve moving forward.

221
00:14:27,032 --> 00:14:30,536
And if anything, Ukraine
is going to continue

222
00:14:30,536 --> 00:14:34,106
to lose significant numbers
of people every year.

223
00:14:34,440 --> 00:14:38,878
And by the way, the Ukrainians are losing
about 600,000 people a year now.

224
00:14:40,012 --> 00:14:41,714
And there's no good reason to

225
00:14:41,714 --> 00:14:45,751
think that that number is going to change
in any significant way moving forward.

226
00:14:45,951 --> 00:14:50,456
The only caveat to this
is that a good number of the people

227
00:14:50,456 --> 00:14:55,494
who have left Ukraine and moved to Europe
may come back,

228
00:14:55,561 --> 00:14:59,331
and that would, in a very important
way, help

229
00:14:59,632 --> 00:15:04,003
mitigate this problem
or ameliorate this problem somewhat.

230
00:15:04,203 --> 00:15:07,473
But the fact is that Ukraine is suffering

231
00:15:07,506 --> 00:15:10,910
a demographic disaster,
and there is little hope

232
00:15:11,343 --> 00:15:14,513
that this situation can be reversed
in the future.

233
00:15:15,948 --> 00:15:18,951
Second, there's the economic disaster.

234
00:15:19,551 --> 00:15:22,521
First of all,

235
00:15:22,788 --> 00:15:25,991
the Russians are wrecking

236
00:15:26,358 --> 00:15:29,995
infrastructure inside of Ukraine.

237
00:15:30,396 --> 00:15:33,065
As Yulia

238
00:15:33,065 --> 00:15:37,436
Mendel points out,
the energy system has been badly damaged.

239
00:15:37,503 --> 00:15:42,174
It's likely to be destroyed
in large part before the winter.

240
00:15:42,708 --> 00:15:45,477
That's likely to have huge

241
00:15:45,477 --> 00:15:49,949
humanitarian consequences
over the course of the winter.

242
00:15:50,082 --> 00:15:54,253
She also points out
that 90% of the storage sites

243
00:15:54,253 --> 00:15:58,190
inside of Ukraine have been destroyed.

244
00:15:58,557 --> 00:16:02,861
And of course, the transportation network
is being torn apart.

245
00:16:03,195 --> 00:16:06,465
The Russians are targeting gas stations

246
00:16:06,598 --> 00:16:10,703
all across Ukraine, but
especially in the western part of Ukraine.

247
00:16:11,236 --> 00:16:16,842
The Russians have shut down the various
Ukrainian ports on the Black Sea.

248
00:16:16,875 --> 00:16:20,746
And in effect,
Ukraine is now a landlocked country.

249
00:16:20,980 --> 00:16:26,318
So with all this wrecked infrastructure,
you basically have a situation

250
00:16:26,585 --> 00:16:29,722
where Ukraine's economy is

251
00:16:29,822 --> 00:16:33,559
incapable of functioning in a way

252
00:16:34,493 --> 00:16:38,063
that other economies in Europe function.

253
00:16:38,130 --> 00:16:42,735
It's become
a completely dysfunctional economy.

254
00:16:43,002 --> 00:16:47,039
And this leads to the second point
that she makes, which is that

255
00:16:47,039 --> 00:16:50,542
Ukraine is now dependent on Western

256
00:16:50,542 --> 00:16:55,381
aid to stay afloat because Ukraine's

257
00:16:55,414 --> 00:17:00,619
economy by itself
can't meet the demands of the war

258
00:17:00,753 --> 00:17:05,591
or the demands of the people,
and can't keep the government afloat.

259
00:17:05,591 --> 00:17:10,396
It depends
to a great extent on aid from the West.

260
00:17:10,629 --> 00:17:14,533
And I would estimate up to now
that the West has given

261
00:17:14,666 --> 00:17:18,137
Ukraine somewhere between 350 billion

262
00:17:18,137 --> 00:17:21,473
and $400 billion in aid.

263
00:17:21,507 --> 00:17:23,742
This is a remarkable number.

264
00:17:23,742 --> 00:17:26,678
Last year,

265
00:17:26,678 --> 00:17:32,251
it was decided that it would be necessary
to keep Ukraine afloat,

266
00:17:32,317 --> 00:17:37,322
to give it about $105 billion,
which could be used

267
00:17:37,823 --> 00:17:41,293
in both 2026 this year and next year,

268
00:17:41,293 --> 00:17:46,598
2027, to pay the bills. And

269
00:17:48,100 --> 00:17:49,034
that basically

270
00:17:49,034 --> 00:17:52,771
meant that you would need
$52 billion this year

271
00:17:52,771 --> 00:17:57,242
for Ukraine and $52
billion next year for Ukraine.

272
00:17:57,242 --> 00:18:00,212
And that money, of course, was allocated.

273
00:18:00,612 --> 00:18:04,483
But what recently happened
is that Ukraine

274
00:18:05,117 --> 00:18:08,787
discovered that it needs 27 million,

275
00:18:08,921 --> 00:18:11,890
billion, 27 billion more dollars

276
00:18:11,957 --> 00:18:14,960
just to make it to the end of this year.

277
00:18:15,160 --> 00:18:17,796
So that $105 billion

278
00:18:17,796 --> 00:18:22,034
that was designed to cover
2026 and 2027 is not sufficient.

279
00:18:22,067 --> 00:18:24,903
You need another $27 billion.

280
00:18:24,903 --> 00:18:27,473
And very important what happened

281
00:18:27,473 --> 00:18:31,076
is that the Europeans began to say

282
00:18:31,910 --> 00:18:34,680
that it is not clear

283
00:18:34,680 --> 00:18:38,016
that we can raise $27 billion.

284
00:18:38,584 --> 00:18:42,855
We've been stretched to the limit
for most,

285
00:18:43,021 --> 00:18:48,160
for the most part, and digging up
another $27 billion on top of the $105

286
00:18:48,160 --> 00:18:52,831
billion that we've already given you,
is probably not possible.

287
00:18:53,132 --> 00:18:59,071
But even if they do come up with the $27
billion, what you see is happening here

288
00:18:59,304 --> 00:19:02,574
is that the money from
the West is drying up.

289
00:19:02,741 --> 00:19:07,146
And of course, President Trump
has made it clear that he has no interest

290
00:19:07,146 --> 00:19:10,682
over the long term of continuing
to sustain

291
00:19:11,049 --> 00:19:13,852
the flow of aid

292
00:19:13,852 --> 00:19:17,623
to Ukraine that we have been giving up to now.

293
00:19:17,656 --> 00:19:19,491
He wants to cut back.

294
00:19:19,491 --> 00:19:22,494
He wants the Europeans to pick up
more of the slack.

295
00:19:22,594 --> 00:19:26,431
He wants the burden of providing
financial aid

296
00:19:26,665 --> 00:19:30,802
to Ukraine,
to fall on the shoulders of the Europeans.

297
00:19:30,802 --> 00:19:33,772
And he wants to get the Americans
out of the business

298
00:19:33,772 --> 00:19:37,276
of supporting the Ukrainians financially.

299
00:19:37,709 --> 00:19:41,780
But the Europeans, of course,
are not in a position to do that.

300
00:19:41,847 --> 00:19:45,851
The Europeans are not, in my opinion,
going to be able to raise

301
00:19:45,851 --> 00:19:50,289
$27 billion more than the $105 billion

302
00:19:50,322 --> 00:19:54,459
they've allocated for 2026 and 2027.

303
00:19:54,593 --> 00:19:58,530
So you see,
when we talk about the economic dimension

304
00:19:59,464 --> 00:20:03,435
of this problem, that what's happened here
is that the infrastructure

305
00:20:04,136 --> 00:20:07,172
in Ukraine has been in large part
destroyed,

306
00:20:07,339 --> 00:20:11,376
therefore its economy has been destroyed,
and therefore it has to depend

307
00:20:11,977 --> 00:20:14,980
to a great extent on Western aid.

308
00:20:14,980 --> 00:20:18,483
And that Western aid is not enough.

309
00:20:18,550 --> 00:20:20,986
And it's beginning to dry up.

310
00:20:22,788 --> 00:20:25,791
Now, one other point on this,

311
00:20:26,491 --> 00:20:28,961
Yulia Mendel points out that

312
00:20:28,961 --> 00:20:31,930
if you look at the debt level

313
00:20:32,030 --> 00:20:35,601
in Ukraine, it's 110%

314
00:20:35,667 --> 00:20:39,171
of gross domestic product, GDP,

315
00:20:39,738 --> 00:20:42,908
110% of gross domestic product is

316
00:20:44,376 --> 00:20:49,948
evidence that economy is deeply indebted
and in deep trouble.

317
00:20:50,148 --> 00:20:52,985
And of course, the IMF has said

318
00:20:52,985 --> 00:20:56,321
explicitly
that this situation is unsustainable

319
00:20:56,588 --> 00:21:00,826
and something has to be done
to restructure the debt.

320
00:21:01,159 --> 00:21:02,261
Good luck with that.

321
00:21:02,261 --> 00:21:05,297
Given the fact that it is

322
00:21:05,330 --> 00:21:10,636
quite clear that the Europeans
and the Americans are going to slow down

323
00:21:10,669 --> 00:21:14,773
in terms
of giving aid to Ukraine moving forward.

324
00:21:15,107 --> 00:21:21,013
Now, the next point I want to talk about
is the territorial disaster

325
00:21:21,280 --> 00:21:23,382
that has taken place in Ukraine.

326
00:21:23,382 --> 00:21:27,119
You want to remember what I've said so far
is that there has been a demographic

327
00:21:27,119 --> 00:21:30,822
disaster,
and there has been an economic disaster.

328
00:21:30,989 --> 00:21:33,492
Now, I want to talk
about the territorial disaster.

329
00:21:33,492 --> 00:21:37,195
And you want to keep in mind,
as I talk about the territorial disaster,

330
00:21:37,262 --> 00:21:42,534
that it is linked to the disaster
that I'm just finishing up with. Now,

331
00:21:43,669 --> 00:21:46,672
regarding the territorial disaster.

332
00:21:47,139 --> 00:21:49,975
Ukraine has already lost

333
00:21:49,975 --> 00:21:52,978
20% of its territory.

334
00:21:52,978 --> 00:21:55,981
The Russians have annexed four oblasts

335
00:21:56,548 --> 00:21:58,984
and they have annexed Crimea.

336
00:21:58,984 --> 00:22:03,388
They've not conquered all the territory
in three of those oblasts,

337
00:22:03,922 --> 00:22:08,860
but nevertheless,
they've annexed four oblasts and Crimea,

338
00:22:09,027 --> 00:22:12,998
and they control about
20% of Ukraine's territory.

339
00:22:13,065 --> 00:22:18,036
That means that Ukraine has lost
a fifth of its territory,

340
00:22:18,236 --> 00:22:23,375
and it has no hope of reconquering
that territory, despite what

341
00:22:23,375 --> 00:22:27,546
one hears in the mainstream media
that 20% is gone.

342
00:22:27,879 --> 00:22:31,550
Now, very importantly,
you want to understand that before

343
00:22:31,550 --> 00:22:36,188
the war, 25% of Ukraine's

344
00:22:36,254 --> 00:22:39,257
GDP was found in that territory,

345
00:22:40,492 --> 00:22:42,394
30% of its

346
00:22:42,394 --> 00:22:45,997
industrial production
was found in that territory.

347
00:22:46,031 --> 00:22:50,135
Here we're talking about the 20%
that Ukraine has lost.

348
00:22:51,036 --> 00:22:56,775
And furthermore, 25% of its population
was located in that territory.

349
00:22:56,842 --> 00:22:59,144
This,
of course, is one of the principal reasons

350
00:22:59,144 --> 00:23:02,381
that Ukraine's population
has shrunk so much,

351
00:23:02,681 --> 00:23:07,719
because that part of the population,
it was located in that eastern

352
00:23:07,719 --> 00:23:11,623
one fifth of Ukrainian territory
that the Russians have now conquered

353
00:23:12,057 --> 00:23:17,195
are no longer counts
as part of the population of Ukraine.

354
00:23:17,896 --> 00:23:21,933
So again,
you see that not only has Ukraine

355
00:23:21,933 --> 00:23:25,637
lost a fifth of its territory,
it's lost territory

356
00:23:25,871 --> 00:23:29,107
that contained industrial
might, that contained GDP

357
00:23:29,307 --> 00:23:32,110
and contained population.

358
00:23:32,110 --> 00:23:35,814
Then to take this
a step further, it's not clear

359
00:23:35,814 --> 00:23:39,451
that Ukraine will not lose more territory.

360
00:23:39,985 --> 00:23:43,388
The Russians make it clear
from time to time

361
00:23:43,522 --> 00:23:46,958
that they are incentivized
to take more territory.

362
00:23:47,492 --> 00:23:50,562
And what is particularly
worrisome from

363
00:23:51,396 --> 00:23:54,399
a Ukrainian point of view
at this point in time

364
00:23:54,666 --> 00:23:57,836
is that the Russians might take Odessa,

365
00:23:58,069 --> 00:24:01,773
and if they take the Odessa Oblast,

366
00:24:01,973 --> 00:24:07,412
that will, in effect permanently
cut Ukraine off from the Black Sea,

367
00:24:07,612 --> 00:24:13,552
and that will have devastating
consequences for the Ukrainian economy

368
00:24:13,618 --> 00:24:18,957
moving forward,
because so much of Ukrainian agricultural

369
00:24:18,957 --> 00:24:23,662
and industrial production
goes out through the Black Sea,

370
00:24:23,795 --> 00:24:28,266
and huge numbers of imports
come in through the Black Sea.

371
00:24:28,400 --> 00:24:32,737
So if the Russians control Odessa
or they take over Odessa

372
00:24:33,104 --> 00:24:35,974
and they annex Odessa, this means

373
00:24:35,974 --> 00:24:39,744
that Ukraine will be permanently
a landlocked country,

374
00:24:39,811 --> 00:24:43,315
which will have devastating
economic consequences.

375
00:24:43,515 --> 00:24:46,518
To go back to the 20% number,
as I've said,

376
00:24:46,918 --> 00:24:50,555
and almost everybody agrees on this,
Ukraine has lost about 20%

377
00:24:50,555 --> 00:24:54,426
of its population,
excuse me, 20% of its territory.

378
00:24:55,494 --> 00:24:58,563
I would
estimate that there's a reasonable chance

379
00:24:58,663 --> 00:25:01,900
that it will end up losing 40%

380
00:25:01,900 --> 00:25:05,670
or 35% of its territory.

381
00:25:06,238 --> 00:25:07,706
It remains to be seen.

382
00:25:07,706 --> 00:25:13,778
But given the direction that the war
is taking, it is clearly possible

383
00:25:14,012 --> 00:25:19,217
that Ukraine will end up losing much more
than just 20% of its territory,

384
00:25:19,384 --> 00:25:24,122
which will have a significant effect
on its GDP moving forward, on its

385
00:25:24,122 --> 00:25:27,659
population size moving forward and on its

386
00:25:27,659 --> 00:25:30,662
industrial production moving forward.

387
00:25:31,696 --> 00:25:34,332
Now, let's talk about

388
00:25:34,332 --> 00:25:38,603
the political dimension of this conflict

389
00:25:38,937 --> 00:25:43,475
and elaborate on why
this is a political disaster.

390
00:25:44,142 --> 00:25:46,578
First of all, it's very clear, as Yulia

391
00:25:46,578 --> 00:25:49,981
Mendel emphasizes that this war

392
00:25:50,348 --> 00:25:54,252
and the continuation of this war, year
after year,

393
00:25:54,853 --> 00:25:57,856
has undermined democracy.

394
00:25:57,923 --> 00:26:01,626
There's great emphasis
placed on censorship

395
00:26:01,793 --> 00:26:05,864
and curtailing free speech
inside of Ukraine.

396
00:26:05,864 --> 00:26:07,999
There is no.

397
00:26:07,999 --> 00:26:11,036
The election that was scheduled

398
00:26:11,036 --> 00:26:14,940
a year ago was deferred,

399
00:26:14,940 --> 00:26:18,543
and there's no evidence there's
going to be an election anytime soon.

400
00:26:18,977 --> 00:26:21,546
And political rights

401
00:26:21,546 --> 00:26:24,549
more generally have been curtailed.

402
00:26:24,716 --> 00:26:29,654
This is hardly surprising
any time a country fights a total war.

403
00:26:30,121 --> 00:26:34,826
And this was true of all of the countries
in World War One, in World War Two.

404
00:26:35,026 --> 00:26:38,563
The government goes to great lengths
to curtail democracy.

405
00:26:38,863 --> 00:26:44,336
You find yourself engaged in
what is sometimes called a total war.

406
00:26:44,669 --> 00:26:47,305
And when you're engaged in a total war,

407
00:26:48,640 --> 00:26:53,378
democracy is almost invariably undermined.

408
00:26:53,678 --> 00:26:57,616
And for sure, the Ukrainians are involved
in in a total war.

409
00:26:57,682 --> 00:26:59,651
This is an existential war for them.

410
00:26:59,651 --> 00:27:03,722
They're fighting for their life,
and they're doing everything they can

411
00:27:03,722 --> 00:27:07,759
to mobilize the country to win this war.

412
00:27:07,859 --> 00:27:12,797
And when that happens, whether it's
Ukraine or Germany or Britain in World War

413
00:27:12,797 --> 00:27:18,503
One or even the United States, democracy
is undermined in very important ways,

414
00:27:18,603 --> 00:27:21,906
which is why you want to minimize
the number of times you fight wars.

415
00:27:21,906 --> 00:27:23,174
And if you do fight wars,

416
00:27:23,174 --> 00:27:27,412
to spend as little time as possible
fighting those wars, because

417
00:27:28,146 --> 00:27:32,384
creating a national security state
and fighting wars all the time,

418
00:27:32,384 --> 00:27:37,589
and especially fighting existential wars,
is bound to undermine democracy.

419
00:27:37,622 --> 00:27:42,394
And unsurprisingly, Ukraine,
which was a flawed democracy

420
00:27:42,427 --> 00:27:45,830
going into the war in 2022,

421
00:27:45,830 --> 00:27:48,833
has seen its democratic institutions

422
00:27:48,833 --> 00:27:52,237
eroded in seriously ways, serious ways.

423
00:27:52,237 --> 00:27:56,441
And this, of course,
will be very difficult to recover from.

424
00:27:56,641 --> 00:28:01,079
One other, very important issue here,
when we talk about what

425
00:28:01,112 --> 00:28:05,183
a political disaster
this war is, has to do with corruption. As

426
00:28:05,283 --> 00:28:09,120
almost everybody knows
from reading the newspaper every day,

427
00:28:09,320 --> 00:28:14,359
there is a huge amount of corruption
inside of Ukraine

428
00:28:14,592 --> 00:28:16,761
and all of this Western aid.

429
00:28:16,761 --> 00:28:19,531
Remember
I was talking about somewhere between 350

430
00:28:19,531 --> 00:28:23,835
to $400 billion
in aid coming into Ukraine.

431
00:28:23,868 --> 00:28:29,708
All of this aid just lends itself
to corruption at the elite level.

432
00:28:29,908 --> 00:28:33,645
And of course, the Ukrainians
have not disappointed us on this front.

433
00:28:33,678 --> 00:28:37,115
There is significant corruption.

434
00:28:37,215 --> 00:28:41,519
So you see, this is this war
has been a political disaster

435
00:28:41,920 --> 00:28:45,123
because of what it means

436
00:28:45,123 --> 00:28:49,160
for democratic institutions
and because of what it means for

437
00:28:50,295 --> 00:28:52,697
jacking up the levels of corruption,

438
00:28:52,697 --> 00:28:56,534
which of course, were high
before the war even started.

439
00:28:56,601 --> 00:29:00,572
I mean, Ukraine was known
as a highly corrupt state

440
00:29:00,638 --> 00:29:05,577
before February 2022,
and that situation has just gotten worse

441
00:29:05,577 --> 00:29:09,347
at the elite level for sure
since the war started.

442
00:29:10,215 --> 00:29:11,549
Excuse me.

443
00:29:11,549 --> 00:29:15,453
Now let me talk about
the security dimension and explain to you

444
00:29:15,520 --> 00:29:18,590
why this has been a security disaster.

445
00:29:18,790 --> 00:29:21,793
And I want to make two major points here.

446
00:29:22,026 --> 00:29:26,431
The first
is that Ukraine, for purposes of security,

447
00:29:27,098 --> 00:29:31,736
wants very much
to become a member of NATO.

448
00:29:32,203 --> 00:29:34,773
And if it can't become a member of NATO,

449
00:29:34,773 --> 00:29:38,343
it wants a security guarantee
from the United States.

450
00:29:39,544 --> 00:29:40,578
It's quite clear.

451
00:29:40,578 --> 00:29:43,615
And Yulia Mendel says this explicitly,

452
00:29:43,882 --> 00:29:47,819
that the question of Ukraine joining
NATO is off the table.

453
00:29:48,019 --> 00:29:51,055
Ukraine is not going to join

454
00:29:52,023 --> 00:29:53,358
NATO, and

455
00:29:53,358 --> 00:29:57,095
it's not going to get a security guarantee
from the United States

456
00:29:57,162 --> 00:30:01,733
or a security guarantee of any consequence
from any European country.

457
00:30:02,267 --> 00:30:05,270
So Ukraine is going to be on its own.

458
00:30:05,403 --> 00:30:08,473
This war, which was fought in large part

459
00:30:08,540 --> 00:30:13,178
so that Ukraine could become
part of NATO, is a failure.

460
00:30:13,278 --> 00:30:16,848
Ukraine is not going to become a part of
NATO.

461
00:30:16,881 --> 00:30:19,584
It's not going to get
a meaningful security guarantee.

462
00:30:19,584 --> 00:30:22,954
And that is to say it's
going to be on its own.

463
00:30:22,987 --> 00:30:26,558
It's going to have to provide
for its own security.

464
00:30:27,392 --> 00:30:30,261
My second major point here,

465
00:30:30,261 --> 00:30:34,465
under the security dimension, is that Ukraine,

466
00:30:34,699 --> 00:30:37,535
is going to end this war

467
00:30:37,535 --> 00:30:40,972
much weaker than when it started the war.

468
00:30:41,906 --> 00:30:46,411
Now, the key point
you want to keep in mind is the two

469
00:30:47,712 --> 00:30:50,682
building blocks of military power.

470
00:30:50,682 --> 00:30:55,320
The two building blocks of military power
are population size.

471
00:30:55,420 --> 00:30:56,454
Number one.

472
00:30:56,454 --> 00:30:59,390
And wealth number two,

473
00:30:59,390 --> 00:31:01,860
to generate military power.

474
00:31:01,860 --> 00:31:05,997
And of course, Ukraine
needs military power to protect itself.

475
00:31:06,030 --> 00:31:09,901
Remember, there's
going to be no membership in NATO.

476
00:31:10,034 --> 00:31:14,372
There's going to be no security guarantee
from the United States

477
00:31:14,372 --> 00:31:15,440
or any other country.

478
00:31:15,440 --> 00:31:20,178
Ukraine is on its own,
so it's going to need a powerful military

479
00:31:20,211 --> 00:31:25,149
or as powerful a military as it can build
to provide for its own security.

480
00:31:25,216 --> 00:31:28,820
But what I'm telling you is
that it's not going to be able

481
00:31:28,820 --> 00:31:31,856
to build a powerful military,
because the two building

482
00:31:31,856 --> 00:31:35,760
blocks of military power
are population size and wealth.

483
00:31:35,827 --> 00:31:38,630
And we talked about population size.

484
00:31:38,630 --> 00:31:43,468
We talked about the demographic disaster
that Ukraine is facing.

485
00:31:43,735 --> 00:31:46,704
And with regard to wealth,

486
00:31:46,704 --> 00:31:51,943
we talked about the economic disaster
that Ukraine is facing.

487
00:31:52,577 --> 00:31:56,581
So you see that
from a security perspective.

488
00:31:56,781 --> 00:32:00,652
Ukraine is in an absolutely horrible,

489
00:32:01,719 --> 00:32:03,254
horrible condition.

490
00:32:03,254 --> 00:32:06,057
It's in an absolutely horrible condition.

491
00:32:06,057 --> 00:32:10,561
So let me just put all the pieces together
and review what I've said to you here

492
00:32:10,595 --> 00:32:12,730
from a demographic point of view.

493
00:32:12,730 --> 00:32:16,868
This is a country that's half the size
it was when it got its independence

494
00:32:16,868 --> 00:32:18,670
in 1991.

495
00:32:18,670 --> 00:32:23,975
And if you look at what's happening
in terms of the birth rate

496
00:32:23,975 --> 00:32:30,315
and the death rate, this is a country
that is continuing to shrink in size.

497
00:32:30,782 --> 00:32:34,719
This is a demographic disaster
that Ukraine is facing.

498
00:32:34,786 --> 00:32:38,423
Furthermore,
it is facing an economic disaster.

499
00:32:38,423 --> 00:32:41,359
Its infrastructure,
its economy has been destroyed.

500
00:32:41,359 --> 00:32:45,496
It's heavily
dependent on support from the West.

501
00:32:46,197 --> 00:32:50,435
And that support is drying up.
Furthermore,

502
00:32:50,435 --> 00:32:54,305
from a territorial point of view,
it's lost 20% of its population.

503
00:32:54,305 --> 00:32:58,376
That population contained
all sorts of wealth, all sorts of people,

504
00:32:58,476 --> 00:33:01,279
all sorts of industrial production.
It's gone.

505
00:33:01,279 --> 00:33:05,283
And it's not clear that 20% will be
all the territory that it loses.

506
00:33:05,283 --> 00:33:09,921
It may lose somewhere in the order
of 35 to 40% of its territory.

507
00:33:10,555 --> 00:33:12,623
The war has been a political disaster.

508
00:33:12,623 --> 00:33:15,560
It's undermined
the democratic institutions

509
00:33:15,560 --> 00:33:18,596
inside of Ukraine,
which were never too strong to begin with.

510
00:33:18,997 --> 00:33:22,433
And furthermore,
it's fueled corruption at the elite level.

511
00:33:22,667 --> 00:33:26,170
And then finally, as we just talked
about at the security level,

512
00:33:26,304 --> 00:33:29,307
this has been a disaster there as well.

513
00:33:29,340 --> 00:33:31,109
Ukraine's not going to join NATO.

514
00:33:31,109 --> 00:33:33,144
It's not going to get
a security guarantee.

515
00:33:33,144 --> 00:33:37,882
And militarily, militarily,
it's going to be weaker moving forward.

516
00:33:37,882 --> 00:33:43,187
Its ability to generate military power
today is much less

517
00:33:43,421 --> 00:33:46,958
than it was in 1991, for sure.

518
00:33:47,158 --> 00:33:51,896
And in 2022,
right before this war started as well.

519
00:33:52,296 --> 00:33:58,269
So this war has been
an unmitigated disaster for Ukraine.

520
00:33:58,269 --> 00:34:01,839
And this,
of course, is why Yulia Mendel is arguing

521
00:34:01,873 --> 00:34:04,876
that Zelensky's continuation of this war

522
00:34:05,376 --> 00:34:09,013
is leading to national suicide.

523
00:34:09,280 --> 00:34:12,984
I think the evidence, when you look at it
carefully, is overwhelming

524
00:34:13,384 --> 00:34:15,420
that she is correct.

525
00:34:15,420 --> 00:34:17,955
Now, I want to conclude
with two final points.

526
00:34:19,023 --> 00:34:19,824
First, I want to

527
00:34:19,824 --> 00:34:23,227
compare this to the situation in Russia.

528
00:34:23,661 --> 00:34:28,733
As you know, I was in Russia
between September 5th and September 12th,

529
00:34:28,733 --> 00:34:34,338
and I spent a lot of time
talking to people and looking around

530
00:34:34,372 --> 00:34:37,775
and assessing
what the situation is in Russia.

531
00:34:38,242 --> 00:34:41,612
And when I read Mendel's piece,
I couldn't help

532
00:34:41,612 --> 00:34:44,816
but think about the contrast with Russia.

533
00:34:45,183 --> 00:34:48,352
The situation in Russia
is the polar opposite

534
00:34:48,386 --> 00:34:52,356
of the situation in Ukraine.

535
00:34:52,490 --> 00:34:55,793
I don't want to argue
that Russia hasn't suffered

536
00:34:55,960 --> 00:34:58,963
from the war because it certainly has.

537
00:34:59,464 --> 00:35:04,535
But if you think about it carefully,
the situation

538
00:35:04,635 --> 00:35:09,273
is just fundamentally different in Russia
than it is in Ukraine today.

539
00:35:09,540 --> 00:35:13,277
Now, Russia
clearly has a demographic problem

540
00:35:13,277 --> 00:35:17,815
independent of the war,
similar to the demographic problem

541
00:35:17,815 --> 00:35:20,551
that Ukraine had even before the war
started.

542
00:35:20,551 --> 00:35:23,554
Both of these countries
had a demographic problem

543
00:35:23,855 --> 00:35:26,557
before the war, for sure.

544
00:35:26,557 --> 00:35:30,795
But what's happened with the Russians
is they have conquered

545
00:35:30,828 --> 00:35:34,398
a huge swath of territory in Ukraine.

546
00:35:34,665 --> 00:35:38,669
And those people
in that swath of territory

547
00:35:38,903 --> 00:35:43,474
who were previously
Ukrainians have now become Russians.

548
00:35:43,674 --> 00:35:47,145
So as a result of this war,
the Russian population

549
00:35:47,178 --> 00:35:50,815
has increased significantly in size.

550
00:35:51,415 --> 00:35:53,751
Furthermore, in terms of territory,

551
00:35:54,752 --> 00:35:57,655
Ukraine has lost 20% of its territory.

552
00:35:57,655 --> 00:36:00,291
Well, who has captured that territory?

553
00:36:00,291 --> 00:36:03,294
The Russians have captured that territory.

554
00:36:03,361 --> 00:36:05,696
So the Russians have gained territory

555
00:36:05,696 --> 00:36:09,500
and gained population
as a result of this war.

556
00:36:10,201 --> 00:36:13,304
And in terms of their security, remember,
I argue that

557
00:36:13,304 --> 00:36:16,307
this war is a security disaster
for Ukraine.

558
00:36:16,674 --> 00:36:19,677
It has not been a security disaster
for Russia.

559
00:36:19,810 --> 00:36:22,880
Even if Russia wins an ugly victory

560
00:36:23,214 --> 00:36:26,517
and Russia pays a price
for fighting this war.

561
00:36:26,918 --> 00:36:32,557
The fact is that militarily,
Russia is in much better shape

562
00:36:32,557 --> 00:36:37,261
today than it was
when the war started in February 2022.

563
00:36:37,461 --> 00:36:42,833
The Russian army is a much more formidable

564
00:36:42,833 --> 00:36:46,337
instrument today than it was in 2022.

565
00:36:46,571 --> 00:36:51,943
And furthermore, Ukraine
is much weaker today than it was in 2022.

566
00:36:52,276 --> 00:36:54,979
If we were to review
what has happened in each

567
00:36:55,980 --> 00:36:58,916
year of this war, what you would see

568
00:36:58,916 --> 00:37:03,854
is that the Ukrainians did very well
against the Russians in 2022.

569
00:37:04,055 --> 00:37:07,992
2022 was the high water
mark for the Ukrainians.

570
00:37:08,259 --> 00:37:13,664
And then in 2023, they launched a major
offensive in June of that year.

571
00:37:13,998 --> 00:37:17,068
And the reason they launched
that major offensive is

572
00:37:17,101 --> 00:37:20,671
they thought that they could effectively
knock the Russians out of the war,

573
00:37:20,938 --> 00:37:25,109
or at least do serious
damage to the Russian military

574
00:37:25,176 --> 00:37:29,680
and Russia's strategic position
in eastern Ukraine.

575
00:37:29,814 --> 00:37:34,518
So in 2023, the Ukrainians felt
they were on a roll.

576
00:37:34,619 --> 00:37:37,622
They had control
of the commanding heights.

577
00:37:38,055 --> 00:37:40,858
But if you look at what happened
that year, towards

578
00:37:40,858 --> 00:37:44,662
the end of that year, 2023,
what happened in 2024,

579
00:37:44,662 --> 00:37:48,833
what happened in 2025,
and where we are in 2026.

580
00:37:48,933 --> 00:37:55,306
You see that Ukraine's security situation
has significantly deteriorated

581
00:37:55,339 --> 00:38:00,344
and Russia's
security situation has improved markedly.

582
00:38:00,911 --> 00:38:03,347
All of this is a way of saying that

583
00:38:03,347 --> 00:38:08,519
Russia is in much better shape today
than it was in 2022.

584
00:38:08,586 --> 00:38:10,821
And again,
I don't want to make light of the fact

585
00:38:10,821 --> 00:38:14,225
that the Russians have suffered
as a result of this war,

586
00:38:14,292 --> 00:38:18,162
that many Russians have died
or been badly wounded,

587
00:38:18,195 --> 00:38:22,633
just as many Ukrainians have died
or have been badly wounded.

588
00:38:22,667 --> 00:38:27,938
But the fact is that the price
that Ukraine has paid up to now,

589
00:38:27,938 --> 00:38:34,712
and will pay in
the future is much, much greater

590
00:38:34,812 --> 00:38:40,518
than the price that the Russians have paid
and will pay moving forward.

591
00:38:41,152 --> 00:38:43,521
My final point, and this is a point

592
00:38:43,521 --> 00:38:46,490
that Mendel makes very clearly,

593
00:38:46,490 --> 00:38:50,394
is it's not just Zelensky
who is responsible

594
00:38:50,561 --> 00:38:53,864
for leading Ukraine toward
national suicide.

595
00:38:54,031 --> 00:38:56,267
It's the West as well.

596
00:38:56,267 --> 00:39:00,137
And as I'm sure almost all viewers know,
the West

597
00:39:00,171 --> 00:39:05,276
has often talked about using Ukraine
as a battering ram

598
00:39:05,976 --> 00:39:09,347
to weaken Russia.

599
00:39:09,880 --> 00:39:13,317
And of course, as Mendel makes clear,

600
00:39:13,351 --> 00:39:17,455
it is the Ukrainians, not the Europeans

601
00:39:18,422 --> 00:39:21,759
nor the
Americans, who are paying the price

602
00:39:22,026 --> 00:39:27,298
for fighting this war
against the Russians.

603
00:39:27,732 --> 00:39:30,234
And she's actually very angry.

604
00:39:30,234 --> 00:39:33,237
And you can see this both in her article

605
00:39:33,304 --> 00:39:36,307
that she wrote in the Weekly Standard

606
00:39:36,440 --> 00:39:40,611
and also in her speech
before the European Parliament.

607
00:39:40,611 --> 00:39:43,614
That was the day after her
article appeared

608
00:39:43,681 --> 00:39:46,717
that she spoke
to the European Parliament.

609
00:39:47,051 --> 00:39:51,021
She talks about people
in the comfortable West.

610
00:39:51,155 --> 00:39:54,158
That's her rhetoric,
people in the comfortable West.

611
00:39:54,558 --> 00:39:58,629
She makes it clear
that she thinks that people in the West,

612
00:39:58,629 --> 00:40:02,099
who are not paying the price
of having to fight against the Russians,

613
00:40:02,600 --> 00:40:04,101
are very comfortable

614
00:40:04,101 --> 00:40:07,872
making the argument that Ukraine
should pay the blood price here.

615
00:40:08,072 --> 00:40:10,908
And this makes her very angry.

616
00:40:10,908 --> 00:40:14,311
And she has this one line
that sticks in my head, which says

617
00:40:14,612 --> 00:40:18,582
that Western political elites would rather

618
00:40:18,582 --> 00:40:22,553
see Russia burn than Ukraine saved.

619
00:40:22,720 --> 00:40:23,554
Think about that.

620
00:40:23,554 --> 00:40:28,192
Western political elites
would rather see Russia burn

621
00:40:29,226 --> 00:40:31,095
than Ukraine saved.

622
00:40:31,095 --> 00:40:34,632
And her point is
that Ukraine is not going to be saved.

623
00:40:34,665 --> 00:40:37,668
It is committing national suicide.

624
00:40:38,068 --> 00:40:42,139
And as I say,
this is a controversial argument for sure.

625
00:40:42,540 --> 00:40:46,110
But I think if you look carefully
at those five dimensions

626
00:40:46,110 --> 00:40:49,280
that I've outlined, what you see is that

627
00:40:49,280 --> 00:40:53,784
Ukraine is facing a disaster
on every one of them.

628
00:40:54,118 --> 00:40:57,521
And this war, in the end, is a complete

629
00:40:57,521 --> 00:41:00,491
catastrophe for Ukraine.

630
00:41:01,058 --> 00:41:05,463
On that sad note,
let me conclude this episode

631
00:41:05,830 --> 00:41:08,866
and wish everybody Godspeed.

632
00:41:09,200 --> 00:41:09,834
Thank you.

